+---
+type: spec
+task_slug: cli-sum-stdin
+status: approved
+created: 2026-10-15
+tags: [timeparse, spec, python, cli, stdin]
+test_framework: pytest
+interview_rounds: 0
+lane: light
+summary: "timeparse CLI: --sum total, '-' reads durations from stdin, all invalid inputs reported"
+---
+
+# SPEC: cli-sum-stdin
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+The `timeparse` CLI only prints one value per duration and stops at the first bad argument. Users want a single total, want to pipe durations in, and want every bad input reported in one run.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+- `--sum` prints one line: the total seconds of all durations.
+- The argument `-` pulls durations from standard input, mixed with normal arguments in order.
+- A run with any invalid input lists every invalid one on stderr, prints nothing on stdout, and returns 2.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### AC-001: Sum of arguments
+**Given** the arguments `--sum 1h 30m`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stdout is exactly `5400\n` and the return value is 0
+
+### AC-002: Stdin input mixed with arguments
+**Given** stdin `"1m\n\n2m\n"` and arguments `- --sum`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stdout is exactly `180\n` and the return value is 0
+**And** `["-", "30s"]` with stdin `"1m\n2m\n"` prints `60`, `120`, `30` (stdin lines sit where `-` sits)
+**And** `["--sum", "-"]` with empty stdin prints `0`; `["--sum", "-", "-"]` with stdin `"1m\n"` prints `60` (stdin read once)
+**And** without `--sum`, `["30s", "-"]` with stdin `"  1m \n\n2m\n"` prints `30`, `60`, `120` in that order (whitespace stripped, blank lines ignored)
+
+### AC-003: Every invalid input is reported
+**Given** the arguments `1h x 2q`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stderr is exactly the two lines `error: invalid duration: 'x'` and `error: invalid duration: '2q'`
+**And** `[" 2q "]` reports `error: invalid duration: '2q'` (stripped text)
+**And** stdout is empty and the return value is 2
+
+### AC-004: Invalid input from stdin, with --sum
+**Given** stdin `" bad \n1m\n"` and arguments `--sum - 2q`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stderr is exactly `error: invalid duration: 'bad'` then `error: invalid duration: '2q'` (input order), stdout is empty, and the return value is 2
+
+### AC-005: Plain output unchanged
+**Given** the arguments `1h 30s` without `--sum`
+**When** `main` runs
+**Then** stdout is `3600\n30\n` and the return value is 0
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- Changes to `parse_duration` or its grammar.
+- Output formats other than integer seconds; other flags.
+- Reading stdin when `-` is absent.
+- argparse usage errors (e.g. no durations at all) and stdin I/O or decode errors keep their default behavior.
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | existing `tests/test_cli.py` uses it; stdin via `monkeypatch.setattr(sys, "stdin", io.StringIO(...))` |
+| Compatibility | Python 3 with `from __future__ import annotations` | matches current module |
+| Signature | `main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int` | unchanged |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| AC-001 | unit | `test_sum_of_arguments` |
+| AC-002 | unit | `test_stdin_mixed_with_args` |
+| AC-003 | unit | `test_reports_every_invalid` |
+| AC-004 | unit | `test_invalid_from_stdin_and_sum` |
+| AC-005 | unit | `test_plain_output_unchanged` |
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+none (defaults chosen, see Refinement Decisions)
+
+## 🔎 Spec Validation
+spec-validator: MAJOR_REVISION (advisory). Critical: the CLI contract change (`--sum`, `-` sentinel, collect-all stderr, exit 2) is not listed as an irreversible decision. DRI call: left `irreversible_decisions: []` because the ask pins the flag names, sentinel and stderr format exactly, so no unit can choose incompatibly; but the collect-all change does replace first-error behaviour, so the DRI should confirm this at `/hm:wrapup`. Warnings addressed: defaults and `-` ordering now pinned in AC-002/AC-003; usage and I/O errors added as non-goals. Suggestion not taken: quoting the ask in oracle_evidence.
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Lane `light`: one file, one session, no irreversible decision (CLI contract is additive and fully pinned by the ask). Interview skipped at autopilot `auto_full`; ask was fully specified.
+- Defaults: stdin is read once, only if `-` appears (a second `-` yields no more lines); `-` with empty stdin contributes no inputs, so `--sum` prints `0`; `--sum` with invalid input still prints nothing and returns 2; the first-error behaviour of `main` is replaced by collect-all; error text is the stripped text for argument inputs as well.
+- Oracle: golden for all ACs, values taken from the user's own examples or hand arithmetic (3600+1800=5400, 60+120=180), independent of the implementation.
